# vllm-2node-dsv41-flash-exl3 - copy to .env and edit.
#
# UNVERIFIED. Every value here is upstream's, except the three marked LOWERED,
# which are lowered for a reason measured on THESE nodes. Nothing in this file
# has been confirmed by a boot on odysseus + poseidon - workspace.yml says why.

# --- what you must set ------------------------------------------------------
# A PATH, NEVER A REPO ID. The overlay's loader joins this string with a
# filename instead of resolving through the Hub, so a repo id fails on a file
# that is present both locally and on the Hub. ./stage-weights.sh --model
# writes this for you.
# MODEL=/home/you/.cache/dsv41-exl3/model

# Rank 0's packed Engram rows live here; on the PEER the same path holds rank
# 1's. Same mount string, different contents - that is what lets one docker
# command run on both ranks. ./stage-weights.sh is what makes that true.
# ENGRAM_PACKED=/home/you/.cache/dsv41-exl3/engram-packed

# --- the memory ladder, and the order matters -------------------------------
# Headroom after warm-up is ~4 GiB per node and the GPU pool IS system RAM, so
# an over-commit does not raise an exception, it takes the host with it
# (docs/decisions.md#persistence-latch is what that looks like afterwards).
# Upstream's HANDOFF.md records a boot that wedged both nodes.
#
# Raise ONE of these at a time, and after each one run a long prefill while
# watching the low-water mark:
#   watch -n5 'free -g; ssh poseidon free -g'
#
#   shipped here     128k context, 2048 chunk, 1 GiB pool   <- upstream's own
#                                                              "first clean boot"
#   upstream's       600k context, 1024 chunk, 2.5 GiB pool <- their validated
#   validated                                                  profile, 2.1 GiB
#                                                              low-water at 601k
#
# Note the direction: their 600k profile uses a SMALLER prefill chunk, because
# the V4.1 indexer's activation peak grows with chunk x context. Raising
# MAX_MODEL_LEN without lowering MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS moves two things at once.
# MAX_MODEL_LEN=131072
# MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=2048
# KV_CACHE_MEMORY_BYTES=1073741824        # 1 GiB ~= 658k tokens at ~1.63 KB/tok
# MAX_NUM_SEQS=2

# LOWERED from upstream's 0.88. With KV_CACHE_MEMORY_BYTES set this is only
# vLLM's startup assertion - MemAvailable at init >= util x 121.69 GiB - not a
# budget. 0.88 demands 107.1 GiB free; ../vllm-2node-glm53-flash-exl3 measured
# 0.87 (105.8 GiB) being REFUSED on these nodes at 104.87 GiB free. Raise it
# only on headless nodes, and only as far as a boot proves.
# GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.86

# Keep MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS - LONG_PREFILL_TOKEN_THRESHOLD >= 256. This is
# what lets a short chat answer during someone else's long prefill: upstream
# measured 216 s -> ~4 s for ~6% off solo prefill.
# LONG_PREFILL_TOKEN_THRESHOLD=1792

# --- speculation, which is a workload choice here rather than a win ----------
# Upstream measured, 2026-09-12, prose:
#   1 stream   k=3  28 tok/s   k=5  25   none 23    -> dspark wins
#   4 streams  none 54 aggregate  >  k=3  42        -> dspark LOSES
# The crossover sits inside this workspace's supported concurrency. Serving
# more than two streams: set none.
# SPEC_METHOD=dspark
# DSPARK_TOKENS=3

# --- EXL3 kernels -----------------------------------------------------------
# Must stay >= MAX_NUM_SEQS x (DSPARK_TOKENS+1), or a decode step stops being a
# single fused launch. At 2 x 4 the floor is 8.
# EXL3_TEMP_ROWS_FUSED=16
# EXL3_FUSED_MOE=1
# EXL3_FAT_GROUPED=1
#
# NOT EXPOSED, deliberately: EXL3_FAT_KERNEL. The E2 fat kernel is K4/MCG-only
# and this is a mul1 K2/K3 tree, so setting it is not a speedup - it is a no-op
# that hides the E3 v2 grouped path that does apply.
#
# NOT EXPOSED EITHER: DSV41_EXL3_SERIAL_STREAMS and
# VLLM_DISABLE_SHARED_EXPERTS_STREAM. Both are hard-set to 1 in up.sh. They are
# deadlock fixes rather than tuning, and a knob implies a choice that is not
# there.

# Upstream tuned 96 on their kit. GB10 has 20 cores, so this is one of the few
# upstream numbers that is about their MACHINE rather than this architecture -
# the reads are NVMe-bound rather than CPU-bound, which is why it survives the
# port unchanged. First knob to question if prefill is slower here than their
# 970 tok/s at 8k.
# DSV41_IO_THREADS=96

# --- topology ---------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT SET, AND NOT AN OVERSIGHT. Upstream pins HEAD_CX7_IF=enp1s0f1np1 and
# WORKER_CX7_IF=enp1s0f0np0. On BOTH our nodes enp1s0f1np1 is DOWN/NO-CARRIER;
# the cabled ports are enp1s0f0np0 and enP2p1s0f0np0, two rails, and
# lib/twonode.sh lets NCCL discover both through ibverbs rather than naming
# one. Copying their pins here would hang ncclCommInitRank.
# Set IB_HCA or IB_GID_INDEX only if a log shows the wrong device chosen.
# IB_HCA=
# IB_GID_INDEX=

# PORT=8897
# IMAGE=ghcr.io/miaai-lab/deepseek-v4.1-flash-exl3-2x-dgx-sparks:2.9bpw
